{"stage":"scope","what":"a REDUCED version of docs/FICTION-CONTROL-PROMPT.md: passage -> analyst -> generator -> measure -> shuffle -> adversary -> score. THE CRITIC IS SKIPPED.","why":"the critic is the governing cost at ~7-14 window points per call; ten calls is most of a 5-hour window and the weekly budget has ~4 points left. Skipping it is a real limitation, not a shortcut to be glossed.","consequence":"this measures the GENERATOR's output on unknowable content, not the pipeline's shipped output. It must not be compared against the shipped sections, which are post-critic."}
{"stage":"comparator","chosen":"runs/tier4-control clean group, 40%","why":"both are fiction, both carry zero domain knowledge, and both are unreviewed-by-critic. The clean group was hand-authored to sit inside the R8/R9 band, so if anything it is MORE polished than raw generator output; that asymmetry runs against the pipeline, and should be stated when reporting.","also_reported":"25% chance, for the absolute level"}
{"stage":"pre-registered-interpretation","table":[
 {"result":"~25%","reading":"the generator's output on unknowable content is at chance. Strong evidence the pipeline does not leak structurally, and that the real sections' 78-100% is knowledge."},
 {"result":"~40%, near the hand-authored clean-fiction floor","reading":"the generator adds nothing beyond the irreducible inference premium a four-option question carries. Same conclusion as above, slightly weaker."},
 {"result":"meaningfully above 40%, say >=55%","reading":"the generator itself leaks on content nobody can know. That is a pipeline defect and the highest-priority finding in the project."}]}
{"stage":"pre-registered-limits","items":[
 "n is at most 8 questions x 3 seeds = 24 trials. The 95% interval on a 40% estimate at 24 trials is roughly +/-20 points. '~40%' and '~55%' may well NOT be separable at this n, and if they are not, the honest report is that the run was underpowered -- not a point estimate presented as an answer.",
 "one generator call, one model, one fabricated passage. A passage that happens to be easy or hard moves the whole number.",
 "the passage is judged by the orchestrator for whether it is genuinely unguessable; that judgement is a single fallible read and is recorded so it can be overturned.",
 "skipping the critic means this says nothing about whether critic rewrites increase or decrease leakage."]}
{"stage":"stop-rule","rule":"the passage is verified BEFORE any downstream spend, and the interpretation above is not edited after results are seen. If the passage fails verification it is re-spawned once; if it fails twice the run is abandoned and reported as abandoned."}
{"stage":"passage","agent":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","words":1576,"domain":"invented sociology of ensemble stage performance -- 'undercraft theory', Kasch, the Fen index, the Corvide Nine","verified_by":"orchestrator, read directly, not taken from the agent's own notes","verdict":"PASS","checks":{"coherent_and_inferable":"yes -- every claim follows from something stated","counterintuitive_claims":"5 delivered against 4 asked, and they are real reversals stated explicitly: projection and undercraft NEGATIVELY associated; the anchor position goes to the WEAKEST projector; audience 'gloss' can rise while real performance falls; troupe quality is non-monotonic in size; a high rescue rate with flat correction load is a WARNING not a strength","discrimination_pairs":"5 given against 3 asked","terminology_invented":"yes, and no overlap with the existing tier4-control passage"}}
{"stage":"passage-risk","recorded_before_results","what":"the passage author flagged its own weakest points unprompted, and I agree with its ranking","items":["the projection/undercraft category split is loosely evocative of the informal real distinction between stage presence and stagecraft. The SPLIT may feel familiar; every specific claim built on it is invented and mostly counterintuitive.","the Fen index is a generic successes-over-attempts ratio, structurally like a save percentage. Generic shape, no specific real theory imported.","STRONGEST RISK: the non-monotonic 'core band' effect. Inverse-U is a pattern a test-wise guesser can apply as a heuristic without reading anything. If this run comes back anomalously high, that section is the first place to look."],"note":"logging the suspected leak site BEFORE seeing results is the point of writing it here"}
