{"stage":"defect","severity":"contract","what":"the generator wrote its trailing {note} AFTER the array's closing bracket, producing two concatenated top-level JSON values, which is not valid JSON and made the file unreadable","cause":"my brief says 'a JSON array of candidates, optionally followed by a trailing {note}', which reads two ways. The 2026-09-19 sections put the note INSIDE the array; this run put it outside. Same brief, both behaviours.","fix":"parseJsonValues() -- the script accepts both. It is a parser, not a repair: it never edits a character, it only finds where one top-level value ends and the next begins, tracking strings and escapes so a brace inside a stem cannot desynchronise the scan.","no_text_touched":true,"ok":false}
